1. Introduction to AWT
What is AWT?
AWT (Abstract Window Toolkit) is Java's original platform-dependent windowing, graphics, and user-interface widget toolkit.

Key Characteristics:
1.Platform-dependent - Uses native OS components
2.Heavyweight components - Each component has a native peer
3.Part of Java Foundation Classes (JFC)
4.Simpler but more limited than Swing

